{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>One who loves silver.</b> His soul is not sated." "<b>And one who loves abundance, not produce.</b> There is one who loves to gather wealth in garments and kinds of merchandise, and does not love produce — this too is vanity, and it reverts upon <b>one who loves silver</b>, that is, the one who gathers silver and gold alone. And there are those who say: <b>one who loves abundance, not produce</b> — 'abundance' means acquiring servants and maidservants and many attendants, and the meaning is that he loves to have a multitude before him."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "I read וגם ישוב על as 'and it too reverts upon,' i.e., this case falls back under the same critique as 'one who loves silver'; the phrase is elliptical and the syntax is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:45.282429528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}